# <Name>

> Template — copy to `tests/stamps/YYYYMMDD_NNN_<name>.md`, fill the
> fields, then add `name` to the `tests:` list of **`tests/suites/e2e.md`**.
> One stamp format for every test: the one `build/stages/30-test.sh` reads
> (`test-rules.md`). `/test add` walks you through it.

## What this verifies

<the running, BUILT system working across runtimes — a user journey through web + api + worker.>

## How it runs

1. ./build/test (phase 2) starts every runtime in `e2e.md`'s `runtimes:` list —
   `commands.start` from `.claude/runtimes/<name>.md` — waits for each
   `health_check`, runs this test, and stops them all, always.
2. Read the base URL from `RUNTIME_<NAME>_HEALTH_URL` (or your own config);
   never hard-code a port the runtime stamp does not declare.
3. Every runtime listed in `runtimes_required` must also be in `e2e.md`'s
   `runtimes:` list — the suite starts runtimes, the stamp documents need.

`run_command` runs from the project root and must exit non-zero on failure.
Run it by hand once before adding it to the suite.

